Characterize the resources needed to reconstruct a result (@rc-resources: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @reproducible-computation, #source "../sources/The-Turing-Way.lingua#r_5K6W3KETGFH4N3SDYCB5V0Q3MZ", #source "../sources/Snakemake-Workflows.lingua#r_6FGN565JFTD2FTW69KDCS9BWHS", #source "../sources/Python-Reference.lingua#r_53J5SVX9CRECPQJFX3EAD8NRCZ", #reproducible-computation "../publication/Results-figures-and-explanation.lingua#r_4CYNSA0PMKHVVM82W63AB23VFH") { r_1MPJ0VZA80BTN6QAFEZFM86T3C
**Read:** [The Turing Way — reproducible research, collaboration, and preservation](../sources/The-Turing-Way.lingua#r_5K6W3KETGFH4N3SDYCB5V0Q3MZ), Research Compendia, environments, and project-design material; [Workflow graphs, environments, and execution — Snakemake documentation](../sources/Snakemake-Workflows.lingua#r_6FGN565JFTD2FTW69KDCS9BWHS), resource declarations and execution reporting; [Python tutorial and standard-library references — Python documentation](../sources/Python-Reference.lingua#r_53J5SVX9CRECPQJFX3EAD8NRCZ), the relevant memory/process measurement references.

A scientifically specified workflow can still be practically inaccessible if it needs undocumented memory, storage, run time, network access, or specialized hardware. Report observed resource requirements with a workload and environment. A reader deciding whether to reproduce a study needs more than a dependency list and an optimistic expected duration.

Distinguish peak memory, retained inputs, temporary intermediates, reusable caches, and final outputs. Streaming can reduce memory while changing which operations remain possible. Compression trades storage and processing and adds a format/decoder dependency. Reconstructible derived outputs can be regenerated, but original observations and permitted source editions may be irreplaceable.

Bound the small teaching program explicitly: one megabyte of input, at most 10,000 lots, and bounded decimal strings. It stores the table in memory to keep the example easy to inspect. A production-scale material ledger would require a revised storage/validation design and corresponding tests; removing the bound without examining arithmetic and memory growth is not a complete scale-up.

**Work:** measure resource use for several authorized or original workload sizes. State which measurement tool and definition produced each number. Estimate the storage and time of a fresh reconstruction, including retrieval and environment creation where relevant. Compare a small independently checkable case with the complete study and explain what scientific questions each can answer.

For the final project provide practical instructions for a small reconstruction and an honest account of the full computation's requirements. If a reported result depends on restricted compute or a disappearing service, document that limit and preserve the strongest accessible evidence and alternative checks. Reproducibility includes the material work needed to keep the method usable.

**Continue:** [Generate the report from the identified result and explain its limits](../publication/Results-figures-and-explanation.lingua#r_4CYNSA0PMKHVVM82W63AB23VFH).

**Return:** [Reproducible computational work](../Reproducible-computation.lingua#r_78FWWJDCV0ZGG7VYSPRCWN56DQ).
